  assumed: B-D07 .3 rounds the interest to the ort and names no mode; the instalment's rounding isn't stated: half up for both (mtg_round)
  assumed: B-D07 .4 says equal instalments (annuity) but names no periodic rate: the yearly rate over 12 months, nominal 12 (O:B-5) (mtg_inst.reset)
  assumed: B-HR2 .2 says 12 % of the net to the ort and names no mode (hr2_tax_round)
  assumed: F6: the forecast's own figures, where no notice is published yet (avg_wage_proj, avg_wage_q4)
  assumed: F8: the story's forecast keeps DUKOR 6M at the fixing of 2025-12-31 for 2026 – 2028; a row of the base (not of the scenario forecast), since a scenario row of a base item governs only from the scenario's from, which would make the mortgage's days law-dated (LOAD-LAWDATE) (dukor_6m[2026-06-30], dukor_6m[2026-12-31], dukor_6m[2027-06-30], dukor_6m[2027-12-31], dukor_6m[2028-06-30])
  assumed: the November export's day is not stated: the 2nd of the next month (story) (gap_from, gap_to)
  assumed: the dossier names no overpayment before the 26th rule starts (story, B-HR2 v1; B-D28 lists 2025 only) (overpay_from)
  assumed: the story's forecast for 2026 – 2028, as seen on 2026-01-02 (story.md, The forecast) (fc_arnika_back, fc_arnika_net, fc_bez_day, fc_bez_inv, fc_fee, fc_fee_dom, fc_flr_credit_day, fc_flr_rate, fc_flr_sell_day, fc_from, fc_it_hi, fc_kessel_026_on, fc_kessel_028_on, fc_law_from, fc_law_odds, fc_living, fc_living_dom[first], fc_living_dom[fourth], fc_living_dom[second], fc_living_dom[third], fc_plot, fc_plot_day, fc_power, fc_power_dom, fc_proj_dom, fc_proj_mean, fc_proj_median, fc_proj_sigma, hr3_line)
  assumed: the story's forecast joins the base's defs: its revenue and VAT (F1, F2), F7's law draw (flat_rate.drawn, kessel_day.f5, out_vat.fc, rev_part.fc)
